    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Soils were collected at the Teller 27 and BEO field sites on August 2nd, 2024, and August 6th, 2024, respectively (Supplemental Figure 1). Samples in the organic layer were collected volumetrically using a serrated knife. In the mineral layer, samples were collected with a split soil corer (diameter 5 cm). At Teller 27, soil cores were collected at high, mid, and low elevation in relation watershed\u2019s topography, with three replicates at each elevation level. Teller 27 cores were sampled at the organic layer, first 5 cm, then every 15 cm until varying constraints including 1) the length of the core, 2) the depth to the water table, 3) the depth to coarse gravel, or 4) depth to the permafrost (Figure 1); exact sample depths are recorded in the dataset. At the BEO, two locations were sampled at depths 0-2, 2-6, 6-12, 12-20, 20-32, 32-48 or until permafrost depth. All sample locations were recorded with Avenza Maps using a mobile device.",
      "Field samples were analyzed at Desert Research Institute Soil Characterization and Quaternary Pedology Laboratory using the pipette method for particle size distribution for sand, silt, and clay composition and the loss-on-ignition method for organic matter content. Samples that did not have enough material for the particle size pipette method used the optical method with a laser particle size analyzer (Mastersizer 3000+ Hydro, Malvern Panalytical, Malvern, UK."
    ],
